// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`builtin skills > L1 prompt text (snapshot) fits the budget 1`] = `
"Skills (abilities the user installed). Each line is "name: what it does". When one fits the request, call use_skill with its name to load its instructions before acting; never guess them.
- clean-downloads: Sorts the Downloads folder into subfolders by file type, after showing the plan and getting an OK. Use when: The user asks to clean up, tidy or sort their Downloads folder.
- export-for-youtube: Exports the open video project as a YouTube-ready MP4 (H.264, 1080p or 4K) from DaVinci Resolve or Blender. Use when: The user asks to export, render or make a YouTube version of their edit or animation.
- fill-this-form-from-profile: Fills in the form on screen from the user's saved profile (name, address, email, phone), with their OK for each field. Use when: The user asks to fill in, complete or auto-fill a form with their details.
- make-text-bigger-here: Makes text bigger in the app in front with its own zoom, or for all of Windows when the user wants that. Use when: The user says text is too small, or asks to zoom in or make things bigger.
- morning-briefing: Opens the user's calendar and mail and reads out today's events and the newest unread emails. Use when: The user says good morning or asks what is on today, their schedule or their briefing.
- read-this-aloud: Reads the selected text, or the main text in the foreground window, out loud. Use when: The user asks to read something aloud, read it to them, or read the screen.
- reply-to-this-email: Drafts a reply to the open email and types it into the reply box. Never sends it. Use when: The user asks to reply to, answer or respond to the email on screen.
- screenshot-and-explain: Looks at the whole screen and explains in plain words what is shown and what the user can do next. Use when: The user asks what they are looking at, what this is, or what something on screen means.
- summarize-this-page: Sums up the web page, document or email in front of the user in a few plain sentences. Use when: The user asks for a summary, the gist or a tl;dr of what is on screen."
`;
